    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<p>Port Aransas sits on the north end of Mustang Island in Nueces County, between the Gulf of Mexico and Corpus Christi and Redfish bays, reached by the ferry from Aransas Pass or by Highway 361 and the JFK Causeway. As a public adjuster in Port Aransas, TX, we help owners of beach homes, condos, short-term rentals, and island businesses with hurricane, wind, hail, and water-related claims. Corpus Christi Public Adjuster does not keep an office on the island; we come to the property to inspect it.</p>
<p>Island properties face exposure that mainland homes do not: direct Gulf winds, surge from both the beach and the bay side, constant salt air, and blowing sand. Many homes are elevated on pilings with enclosed lower levels, and the island has many multi-story condominium buildings with flat or low-slope roofs, balconies, and sliding glass doors. Salt-air corrosion of fasteners, flashing, and HVAC equipment can complicate a claim, because an insurer may argue that some deterioration is wear and tear rather than storm damage.</p>

<h2>Hurricanes that shaped Port Aransas</h2>
<p><strong>Hurricane Celia (1970):</strong> HURDAT places Celia's Category 4 landfall point in the Port Aransas and Aransas Pass area on August 3, 1970. The <a href="https://www.weather.gov/crp/hurricanecelia" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NWS Corpus Christi Celia page</a> describes the storm.</p>
<p><strong>Hurricane Harvey (2017):</strong> Harvey's Category 4 landfall on San José Island, just across the Aransas Pass channel, hit Port Aransas hard. NCEI's Nueces County summary says <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=720925" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the most significant damage was in Port Aransas, where widespread major damage occurred</a>, with most homes suffering major roof damage and some losing roofs and walls. <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=720926" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Storm tides of 6 to 8 feet</a> entered from the west, from Corpus Christi and Redfish bays, pushing boats out of their moorings onto high ground. That bay-side surge is an important detail: on the island, flood damage does not only come from the beach.</p>
<p><strong>Tropical Storm Harold (2023):</strong> On August 22, 2023, NCEI lists a <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1133838" target="_blank" rel="noopener">48 mph gust at Port Aransas</a> and elevated tides on the barrier islands.</p>

<h2>Hail and thunderstorm wind on the island</h2>
<p>Port Aransas is not immune to severe thunderstorms. On November 1, 2025, the Mustang Island State Park emergency manager estimated <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1297578" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3-inch hail at the Port Aransas airport</a>, the largest hail report in Nueces County's NCEI records. Older events include November 24, 1996, when <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=5569235" target="_blank" rel="noopener">roofs were damaged on several businesses and two trailers were blown off their foundations</a>, and September 12, 2003, when a <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=5371534" target="_blank" rel="noopener">condo complex security building had major damage</a> and several homes had roof damage. Large hail can crack tile, dent metal roofing, break skylights, and damage rooftop units, so our <a href="/services/hail-damage-claims/">hail damage claims</a> page applies here as much as on the mainland.</p>

